Z||000000||Banzai||12-13-2001||06:35 AM||||I've settled on swapping the 4.9 caddy into my fully restored 84. How does the weight affect handling?? How does it affect ride height?? Will rear coilovers be necessary. I have Eibach Pro-lines and KYB's.<P>Thanks <BR>Banzai !!!!!!!!<p>[This message has been edited by Banzai (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||12-13-2001||10:37 AM||||As I understand it, there is only a slight difference in weight between a 2.8, and 4.9. I don't think there are any great suspension issues involved.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000002||Banzai||12-13-2001||05:08 PM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||12-13-2001||05:14 PM||||What Buzz said was correct. With only a few pounds difference between stock and the 4.9, the stock suspension should work just as well. That's one of the very nice advantages to this swap.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P><B>JUST ADDED: </B>1988 GT w/ T-Tops, 5-Speed, and Performance Sound.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Banzai||12-13-2001||07:05 PM||||Thanks Guys<P>Banzai !!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||12-13-2001||07:35 PM||||The Caddy weighs 371lb. with all the accessories, compare that to the duke @ 302lb, or the 2.8 @ 376lb. Lots of guys put the 3800SC or Chevy in without changing the springs, and they are 445-585lb. On My Cadero coupe I just installed a set of stock '87 GT springs.||||reg||1
Z||000006||cadero2dmax||12-13-2001||07:58 PM||||Don't forget to consider the trans in those weight calculations. Unless you stick with a Fiero trans, the heavier Cad trans throws those numbers off a little. If you use the Th125 and stock axles, well, yes you are about the same.<P>But the Cad auto is heavier than the Fiero's - - can't quote figures because I haven't weighed them. But I would surmise 50lbs More or less. Using a stock Fiero standard still adds over 15lbs for the custom flywheel.<P>Hope this clears that up - - <P>For the suspension, I would suggest 250 to  300lb springs for any of these combos, which could be easiest accomplished with coil-overs.<P>G<BR><p>[This message has been edited by cadero2dmax (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||1
